### c) Description of Dead Material

The amount of dead material in front of TPC differs up to 25% between data and simulation [169]. The symmetric systematic uncertainty on the TPC track reconstruction efficiency due to dead material \(\Delta\epsilon_{\rm TPC}^{\rm DM}\) was introduced as:

\[\Delta\epsilon_{\rm TPC}^{\rm DM}=\pm 0.25\cdot\delta\epsilon_{\rm TPC} \tag{3.11}\]

where \(\delta\epsilon_{\rm TPC}\), estimated with no-pile-up MC, is the amount of lost particles due to the interaction with dead material in front of TPC. The sample distribution of \(\delta\epsilon_{\rm TPC}\) for \(\pi^{-}\) as a function of \(p_{\rm T}\) and \(\eta\) in one \(V_{z}\) bin is shown in Fig. 3.28.

