### 4.8 Systematic Uncertainties

The systematics uncertainties were handled by modifying either the input distributions or the unfolding matrix. Next, the differences between standard and changed bins of the distributions were calculated.

Some of the systematic uncertainties on \(1/N\)\(dN/dn_{\rm ch}\) due to the track reconstruction efficiency were propagated by using a random number from the uniform distribution. If this number is smaller than the absolute value of systematic uncertainty, then \(n_{\rm sel}\) was increased or decreased, depending on the sign of systematic uncertainty. Events with \(n_{\rm sel}=0,1\) do

