## Chapter 5 Comparison of Charged-Particle Densities at Central Rapidities

The measured charged-particle densities in pseudorapidity near \(\eta\approx 0\) are compared to other experimental results from \(pp\) and \(p\bar{p}\) collisions (shown in Fig. 5.1). Various event selections, based on the topology of the final state, allow to split the data samples into enhanced in non-SD (NSD) and SD events, whose sum forms the inelastic sample. For SD events, the midrapidity region is located at \(\bar{\eta}=\eta^{\star}=-\ln(\sqrt{s}/M_{X})\), instead of \(\eta\approx 0\), and the proper energy scale is given by \(M_{X}\) instead of \(\sqrt{s}\). The values of \(\eta^{\star}\) and \(\langle M_{X}\rangle\), calculated separately for STAR and ATLAS data, are presented in Tab. 5.1. For some ranges of \(\xi\), the value of \(\eta^{\star}\) is outside the fiducial region of the measurement. In the case of other experiments the pseudorapidity densities were obtained in the region of the total number of primary charged particles \(n_{\rm ch}\geq 1\) (instead of \(n_{\rm ch}\geq 2\) as in these analyses). Therefore, the results from STAR and ATLAS analyses were extrapolated to the above fiducial region using PYTHIA 8 A2 (MBR) SD and PYTHIA 8 A3 (DL) SD predictions, respectively. The uncertainties due to the corrections are not estimated.

